# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal data — the most important rules in this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NewMe is local-only by design: a user's habit history, notes and
# health-derived values never leave their device (spec §1.5). A backup file
# pulled off a phone for debugging contains exactly that history in plaintext.
# Committing one — especially to a public repo — would be the precise failure
# the whole architecture exists to prevent.
*.newme
newme-backup-*
newme-events-*.csv
newme-habits-*.csv
/snapshots/
/fixtures/personal/

# Local SQLite databases pulled off a device or created by tooling.
# Note: committed test fixtures under src/**/__fixtures__ are re-allowed below.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies & build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
web-build/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
*.hbc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Expo / React Native
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.expo/
.expo-shared/
expo-env.d.ts
.metro-health-check*
.eas-build-local-nodejs/

# Native projects are generated by `expo prebuild` / `expo run`.
# Remove these two lines if you ever adopt the bare workflow and start
# hand-editing native code.
/ios
/android

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signing & credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
credentials.json

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never ignore these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Drizzle migrations are a PERMANENT contract, not build output. Importing a
# two-year-old backup replays the whole chain (spec §8.3.4), and with no
# server there is no way to repair a device remotely. Every migration and its
# journal must be committed, and a shipped one must never be edited — only
# appended to.
!src/data/db/migrations/
!src/data/db/migrations/**

# Golden-file backup fixtures: one per historical schemaVersion, all of which
# must still import on main (spec §8.3.6). These are synthetic, never real
# user data.
!src/**/__fixtures__/
!src/**/__fixtures__/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS & editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.orig
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
